How It Works

1. The battery powers the Arduino Uno and the motor driver.

2. When the power switch is turned ON, the Arduino starts running the uploaded program.

3. The Arduino sends a control signal from Pin D9 to the L298N motor driver.

4. The motor driver supplies power to the DC motor, causing the main rotor to rotate.

5. At the same time, the Arduino controls the red LED (Pin D6) and green LED (Pin D7) to simulate helicopter navigation lights by blinking them in sequence.

6. The helicopter remains stationary while the rotor spins and the LEDs continue blinking until the power is switched OFF.

